Keep a message only when it differs from the message immediately before it in the input (the first message is always kept). One pass, O(n) time.

def dedupe(messages):
    out = []
    for i, m in enumerate(messages):
        if i == 0 or m != messages[i - 1]:
            out.append(m)
    return out

The full set 1..n sums to n(n+1)/2, so the missing number is that total minus the sum of `rolls`. O(n) time, O(1) space. Use a 64-bit integer (n(n+1)/2 is about 5×10^9 for n = 10^5) or XOR 1..n with every recorded value to avoid overflow.

def missing_roll(n, rolls):
    return n * (n + 1) // 2 - sum(rolls)

