            largest = x
        if x < smallest:
            smallest = x
    return largest, smallest

Accumulate the total in one pass, then divide by the element count using real (floating-point) division. O(n) time, O(1) space.

def sum_and_average(arr):
    total = 0
    for x in arr:
        total += x
    return total, total / len(arr)

One pass: an element is even when x % 2 == 0, otherwise odd. Testing `== 0` is safe for negatives, whereas `x % 2 == 1` fails in languages where -3 % 2 is -1 (C, C++, Java, JavaScript). O(n) time, O(1) space.

