Keep a stack of day indices still waiting for a higher price (their prices are non-increasing from bottom to top). For each new price, pop every index with a strictly lower price and record the gap i - j, then push i. Each index is pushed and popped at most once: O(n) time, O(n) space.

def days_until_higher(prices):
    wait = [0] * len(prices)
    stack = []
    for i, p in enumerate(prices):
        while stack and prices[stack[-1]] < p:
            j = stack.pop()
            wait[j] = i - j
        stack.append(i)
    return wait

Count each code with a hash map in O(n). No count can exceed n, so drop codes into buckets indexed by count and read buckets from highest to lowest until k codes are collected: O(n) overall. A size-k min-heap (O(m log k) for m distinct codes) or sorting the distinct codes by count (O(m log m)) is also accepted.

