Bottom-up DP: dp[x] is the fewest coins that make x, with dp[0] = 0 and dp[x] = 1 + min(dp[x - c]) over coins c ≤ x; unreachable amounts stay at infinity and map to -1. O(amount × number of coins) time, O(amount) space. BFS over amounts is also accepted; greedy is wrong.

def min_coins(coins, amount):
    INF = float('inf')
    dp = [0] + [INF] * amount
    for x in range(1, amount + 1):
        for c in coins:
            if c <= x and dp[x - c] + 1 < dp[x]:
                dp[x] = dp[x - c] + 1
    return dp[amount] if dp[amount] != INF else -1

This is the longest window with at most k zeros. Slide a window: extend the right edge, counting zeros; while the count exceeds k, move the left edge right (decrementing when a zero leaves). Track the largest window. O(n) time, O(1) space.

